p: .
t. 
|  CPS can claim even more extraordinary powers over a parent's life. Besides supervising visits, CPS has the power to inspect a parent's home
|  (without obtaining a search warrant). This means that caseworkers may
|  arrive at any time (announced or otherwise), inspect anything, and then
|  make reports that will later appear in court. They can also subject a
|  mother to endless mental health examinations and have broad license
|  to invade her privacy by demanding releases for personal information
.  such as medical reports, therapist's reports, and the like

--- Sentence/end 
