|  energy and time left for parenting.How could a woman's commitment to legal issues such as attempting to protect her child from an apparently abusive relationship
|  constitute child neglect? Here is how CPS
|  built a catch-22 for this particular mother:During custody litigation between the couple (who were never married), the couple's child reportedly showed signs of having been sexually
|  abused. CPS records show that sex abuse referrals were made to the
|  agency by two psychologists, one of whom was the child's therapist. CPS
